1
00:00:02,440 --> 00:00:05,650
MATTHEW: Every school we cover gets one video before March.

2
00:00:06,340 --> 00:00:06,970
MATTHEW: Its best player.

3
00:00:07,720 --> 00:00:08,290
MATTHEW: Its best run.

4
00:00:09,280 --> 00:00:13,750
MATTHEW: Bowling Green goes first, because Bowling Green has a Hall of Famer, and his name is Nate Thurmond.

5
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:15,810
MATTHEW: He grew up in Akron, the Rubber City.

6
00:00:16,380 --> 00:00:18,310
MATTHEW: At Central High he was not even the star.

7
00:00:18,700 --> 00:00:23,090
MATTHEW: He played forward behind an older kid named Gus Johnson, who also ended up in the Hall of Fame.

8
00:00:23,560 --> 00:00:24,590
MATTHEW: Ohio State wanted him.

9
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:26,790
MATTHEW: He did not want to sit behind Jerry Lucas.

10
00:00:27,340 --> 00:00:31,350
MATTHEW: So he took the road west to Bowling Green, to a coach his players called Blinky.

11
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:33,910
MATTHEW: Freshmen could not play varsity back then.

12
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:35,550
MATTHEW: So his first real season was nineteen sixty.

13
00:00:37,060 --> 00:00:39,050
MATTHEW: Bowling Green opened a new arena that December.

14
00:00:39,520 --> 00:00:41,150
MATTHEW: Today it carries the coach's name.

15
00:00:42,020 --> 00:00:43,830
MATTHEW: Year one, the team went ten and fourteen.

16
00:00:44,820 --> 00:00:47,410
MATTHEW: Thurmond averaged seventeen points and seventeen rebounds.

17
00:00:48,020 --> 00:00:49,910
MATTHEW: A losing team with a monster in the middle.

18
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:52,170
MATTHEW: Year two, twenty-one and four.

19
00:00:53,320 --> 00:00:53,930
MATTHEW: Mid-American champions.

20
00:00:54,320 --> 00:00:55,430
MATTHEW: Ranked eighth in the country.

21
00:00:55,860 --> 00:00:58,950
MATTHEW: Then Butler beat them by one point in the NCAA tournament.

22
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:01,550
MATTHEW: Fifty-six, fifty-five.

23
00:01:01,600 --> 00:01:02,170
MATTHEW: Senior year.

24
00:01:02,680 --> 00:01:02,850
MATTHEW: February sixteenth, nineteen sixty-three.

25
00:01:05,480 --> 00:01:07,490
MATTHEW: Number two Loyola comes to Bowling Green.

26
00:01:08,180 --> 00:01:10,510
MATTHEW: Loyola will win the national championship that spring.

27
00:01:11,220 --> 00:01:12,270
MATTHEW: Bowling Green beats them by seventeen.

28
00:01:13,500 --> 00:01:14,650
MATTHEW: Thurmond had twenty-four and twelve.

29
00:01:15,460 --> 00:01:19,290
MATTHEW: His coach called it the greatest team effort he ever saw from a Bowling Green team.

30
00:01:19,980 --> 00:01:20,790
MATTHEW: Another MAC title.

31
00:01:21,240 --> 00:01:23,270
MATTHEW: In the NCAA tournament they beat Notre Dame.

32
00:01:23,660 --> 00:01:26,070
MATTHEW: Thurmond: sixteen points, twenty rebounds.

33
00:01:27,040 --> 00:01:29,170
MATTHEW: Then Illinois ended the dream in East Lansing.

34
00:01:29,820 --> 00:01:30,910
MATTHEW: And here is the part I love.

35
00:01:31,520 --> 00:01:35,490
MATTHEW: His last college game was the regional consolation game, against Mississippi State.

36
00:01:36,120 --> 00:01:40,690
MATTHEW: The night before, Mississippi State had sneaked out of its own state to play integrated Loyola.

37
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:41,850
MATTHEW: The Game of Change.

38
00:01:42,420 --> 00:01:46,130
MATTHEW: Nate Thurmond, Black center from Akron, gets that team the next night.

39
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:48,090
MATTHEW: He grabs thirty-one rebounds.

40
00:01:48,140 --> 00:01:50,030
MATTHEW: Thirty-one.

41
00:01:50,080 --> 00:01:51,830
MATTHEW: It is still the Bowling Green record.

42
00:01:52,220 --> 00:01:57,930
MATTHEW: Two MAC titles, an All-American season, and four hundred fifty-two rebounds as a senior, a school record.

43
00:01:58,420 --> 00:02:00,170
MATTHEW: The Warriors took him third overall.

44
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:01,130
MATTHEW: Part two.

45
00:02:01,460 --> 00:02:01,910
MATTHEW: The pros.

46
00:02:02,220 --> 00:02:04,270
MATTHEW: In San Francisco he backed up Wilt Chamberlain.

47
00:02:04,960 --> 00:02:08,950
MATTHEW: Then the Warriors traded Wilt in nineteen sixty-five, and the middle was Nate's.

48
00:02:09,300 --> 00:02:11,850
MATTHEW: He once grabbed eighteen rebounds in a single quarter.

49
00:02:12,260 --> 00:02:16,090
MATTHEW: In sixty-seven, sixty-eight he averaged twenty points and twenty-two rebounds.

50
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:17,670
MATTHEW: Seven All-Star games.

51
00:02:18,040 --> 00:02:21,910
MATTHEW: Some of the best defense a center ever played.

52
00:02:21,860 --> 00:02:22,190
MATTHEW: Traded to Chicago in seventy-four.

53
00:02:23,360 --> 00:02:27,630
MATTHEW: That October, he records the first official quadruple-double in NBA history.

54
00:02:28,320 --> 00:02:32,390
MATTHEW: Twenty-two points, fourteen rebounds, thirteen assists, twelve blocks.

55
00:02:32,760 --> 00:02:36,090
MATTHEW: Then, in nineteen seventy-five, he comes home to Ohio.

56
00:02:36,600 --> 00:02:37,510
MATTHEW: The Cleveland Cavaliers.

57
00:02:38,200 --> 00:02:42,010
MATTHEW: They played way out in a field in Richfield, between Cleveland and Akron.

58
00:02:42,760 --> 00:02:44,870
MATTHEW: The Cavs were six and eleven when he arrived.

59
00:02:45,260 --> 00:02:47,170
MATTHEW: They went forty-three and twenty-two after.

60
00:02:47,860 --> 00:02:48,790
MATTHEW: Central Division champions.

61
00:02:49,460 --> 00:02:50,630
MATTHEW: Game seven against Washington, eighty-seven to eighty-five.

62
00:02:52,700 --> 00:02:53,910
MATTHEW: The Miracle of Richfield.

63
00:02:53,960 --> 00:02:55,550
MATTHEW: Zero.

64
00:02:55,600 --> 00:02:58,490
MATTHEW: And they lost to Boston after Jim Chones broke his foot.

65
00:02:59,440 --> 00:03:01,610
MATTHEW: Thurmond played one more year and retired in nineteen seventy-seven.

66
00:03:03,100 --> 00:03:05,370
MATTHEW: That December, the Cavaliers retired number forty-two.

67
00:03:06,380 --> 00:03:07,830
MATTHEW: The first number they ever retired.

68
00:03:08,340 --> 00:03:08,530
MATTHEW: Part three.

69
00:03:09,200 --> 00:03:10,090
MATTHEW: Now it goes off the rails.

70
00:03:11,540 --> 00:03:14,450
MATTHEW: I love Nate Thurmond.

71
00:03:14,500 --> 00:03:16,050
MATTHEW: I want that on the record.

72
00:03:16,100 --> 00:03:14,350
MATTHEW: But I also have a spreadsheet.

73
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:17,010
MATTHEW: Here are the Cleveland rafters, drawn to scale.

74
00:03:17,560 --> 00:03:20,370
MATTHEW: Every banner's length is the points that man scored for Cleveland.

75
00:03:21,020 --> 00:03:21,530
MATTHEW: Ilgauskas, ten thousand six hundred.

76
00:03:21,580 --> 00:03:24,890
MATTHEW: Daugherty.

77
00:03:24,940 --> 00:03:24,990
MATTHEW: Carr.

78
00:03:25,700 --> 00:03:25,750
MATTHEW: Price.

79
00:03:26,260 --> 00:03:26,670
MATTHEW: Bingo.

80
00:03:27,340 --> 00:03:27,570
MATTHEW: Nance.

81
00:03:28,020 --> 00:03:28,150
MATTHEW: And forty-two.

82
00:03:28,200 --> 00:03:31,530
MATTHEW: Five hundred sixty-six.

83
00:03:31,580 --> 00:03:33,190
MATTHEW: A hundred and fourteen games in a Cavs uniform.

84
00:03:33,800 --> 00:03:36,490
MATTHEW: The next fewest among their retired numbers is Larry Nance, four hundred thirty-three.

85
00:03:38,900 --> 00:03:39,230
MATTHEW: Banner math.

86
00:03:39,940 --> 00:03:44,310
MATTHEW: It takes nearly nineteen Cleveland Nate Thurmonds to fill one Ilgauskas banner.

87
00:03:45,960 --> 00:03:46,250
MATTHEW: Eighteen point four for Daugherty.

88
00:03:47,180 --> 00:03:48,230
MATTHEW: Even Larry Nance is twelve point eight Thurmonds.

89
00:03:50,040 --> 00:03:52,350
MATTHEW: So is it the thinnest retired number in the league?

90
00:03:52,800 --> 00:03:53,770
MATTHEW: We went through all of them.

91
00:03:54,280 --> 00:03:55,810
MATTHEW: By points with the team, yes.

92
00:03:55,860 --> 00:03:57,330
MATTHEW: Five sixty-six.

93
00:03:57,380 --> 00:03:58,890
MATTHEW: Nobody else we found is under a thousand.

94
00:03:59,840 --> 00:04:02,750
MATTHEW: By games, Malik Sealy in Minnesota has one fewer.

95
00:04:03,480 --> 00:04:08,530
MATTHEW: And to be clear, Sealy, Bobby Phills and Drazen Petrović died while they were still playing.

96
00:04:09,220 --> 00:04:11,390
MATTHEW: Those numbers are not a joke, and neither is this one.

97
00:04:11,660 --> 00:04:12,690
MATTHEW: It just weighs the least.

98
00:04:13,080 --> 00:04:14,090
MATTHEW: Now the whole league.

99
00:04:15,120 --> 00:04:17,510
MATTHEW: Two hundred forty-one retired honors across thirty franchises.

100
00:04:18,120 --> 00:04:18,830
MATTHEW: The Celtics have twenty-five.

101
00:04:19,220 --> 00:04:20,530
MATTHEW: The Clippers have zero.

102
00:04:21,640 --> 00:04:22,570
MATTHEW: Banners per championship.

103
00:04:23,300 --> 00:04:25,270
MATTHEW: Boston hangs about one and a half per title.

104
00:04:25,780 --> 00:04:27,270
MATTHEW: The Lakers, fewer than one.

105
00:04:27,680 --> 00:04:30,110
MATTHEW: Phoenix has seventeen honors and no championship.

106
00:04:30,740 --> 00:04:32,250
MATTHEW: Utah, eleven and none.

107
00:04:32,860 --> 00:04:34,970
MATTHEW: Cleveland, nine honors, one title.

108
00:04:35,460 --> 00:04:39,370
MATTHEW: So pound for pound, forty-two in Cleveland is the lightest banner in basketball.

109
00:04:39,860 --> 00:04:41,690
MATTHEW: And it was the first banner they ever hung.

110
00:04:42,520 --> 00:04:44,470
MATTHEW: For the season Cleveland first believed.

111
00:04:45,060 --> 00:04:45,890
MATTHEW: Nate Thurmond died in twenty sixteen.

112
00:04:46,900 --> 00:04:47,070
MATTHEW: He was seventy-four.

113
00:04:48,220 --> 00:04:53,350
MATTHEW: His number hangs in San Francisco, in Cleveland, and in Bowling Green, where he still owns the glass.

114
00:04:54,420 --> 00:04:54,950
MATTHEW: Thirty-one rebounds.

115
00:04:55,380 --> 00:04:55,830
MATTHEW: Keep it mid.

116
00:04:56,220 --> 00:04:56,710
MATTHEW: Keep it real.
